# oracle: fix graphics/isosurface with a per-atom compute (ke/atom) and an atom-style variable as the property, in a p p f box whose cluster straddles the periodic x face; the neighbor lists are rebuilt only every 20 steps, so during the 10-step NVE run the ghost atoms keep their set and follow their atoms (forward_comm coordinates); STL text at setup and every 5 steps
# oracle-files: w213iso_ke.0.stl w213iso_ke.5.stl w213iso_ke.10.stl w213iso_v.0.stl w213iso_v.10.stl
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p f
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 6 0 6 0 6
create_box      1 box
region          ball sphere 0.0 3.0 3.0 1.8
create_atoms    1 region ball
mass            1 1.0
velocity        all create 2.0 4711 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 20 delay 0 check no
compute         ke all ke/atom
variable        w atom 1.0+0.1*x
fix             1 all nve
fix             iso all graphics/isosurface 5 0.4 1.0 quality min property c_ke filename w213iso_ke.*.stl
fix             iso2 all graphics/isosurface 10 0.8 1.1 quality min property v_w filename w213iso_v.*.stl
thermo          5
thermo_style    custom step temp pe
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             10
